    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "It's a weird issue that I've had for a while but never had the time to investigate properly.\r\nI use LazyVim and with the default provided for navigating hunks with `]h` and `[h` i find it a bit awkward to use so i had keymaps that use `<c-j>` and `<c-k>`.\r\nIssue is when I initially open a buffer and use it it works fine but upon navigating to  to neo-tree window and back it stops working after that.\r\nI suspect this might not be something specific to `mini.diff` but i still wanted to ask here as some more people might've had similar issues.\r\n\r\nThank you!",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It's a weird issue that I've had for a while but never had the time to investigate properly.<br>\nI use LazyVim and with the default provided for navigating hunks with <code class=\"notranslate\">]h</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">[h</code> i find it a bit awkward to use so i had keymaps that use <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;c-j&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;c-k&gt;</code>.<br>\nIssue is when I initially open a buffer and use it it works fine but upon navigating to  to neo-tree window and back it stops working after that.<br>\nI suspect this might not be something specific to <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.diff</code> but i still wanted to ask here as some more people might've had similar issues.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you!</p>",
    "bodyText": "It's a weird issue that I've had for a while but never had the time to investigate properly.\nI use LazyVim and with the default provided for navigating hunks with ]h and [h i find it a bit awkward to use so i had keymaps that use <c-j> and <c-k>.\nIssue is when I initially open a buffer and use it it works fine but upon navigating to  to neo-tree window and back it stops working after that.\nI suspect this might not be something specific to mini.diff but i still wanted to ask here as some more people might've had similar issues.\nThank you!",
