                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> If you have a workaround do tell\r\n\r\nSorry, but the only suggestion I have is to use different keys which do not conflict with one another.\r\n\r\nThe default `[h` and `]h` are in line with common `[` and `]` meaning of \"navigate to previous/next\" something.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you have a workaround do tell</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, but the only suggestion I have is to use different keys which do not conflict with one another.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The default <code class=\"notranslate\">[h</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">]h</code> are in line with common <code class=\"notranslate\">[</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">]</code> meaning of \"navigate to previous/next\" something.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "If you have a workaround do tell\n\nSorry, but the only suggestion I have is to use different keys which do not conflict with one another.\nThe default [h and ]h are in line with common [ and ] meaning of \"navigate to previous/next\" something.",
